 "response": "**Getosti's budget is now $2,095K.**\n\n1. **Which records count:** Under the policy, only Finance Office entries change the budget. Messages from Facilities, PMO, Sales, Engineering and the other teams were ignored. So were Finance Office entries that don't change the budget, such as cost center codes, room moves and audit notes.\n\n2. **Withdrawal chains:** Each chain was resolved from its last link backward. A withdrawal counts only if it was not itself withdrawn by a withdrawal that counts. The decisive examples:\n   - #0002 still applies. Its chain is #0161 \u2192 #0081 \u2192 #0032 \u2192 #0015 \u2192 #0009 \u2192 #0007 \u2192 #0002, so the withdrawal #0007 is undone.\n   - #0003 stays withdrawn. Its chain is #1164 \u2192 #0154 \u2192 #0021 \u2192 #0013 \u2192 #0012 \u2192 #0003, so the withdrawal #0012 is effective.\n   - #0033 stays withdrawn. Its chain is #1438 \u2192 #0784 \u2192 #0708 \u2192 #0534 \u2192 #0165 \u2192 #0033, so #0165 is effective.\n   - #0071 still applies. Its chain is #1250 \u2192 #0150 \u2192 #0087 \u2192 #0080 \u2192 #0071, so #0080 is undone.\n   - #0206, #0339, #0384, #0533 and #0568 stay withdrawn, because their chains also end with the withdrawal in effect.\n   - #0431, #0420, #0712, #0686, #0693 and #0049 still apply, because their withdrawals were undone.\n\n3. **Calculation:** Starting from the $1,730K set in #0001, every remaining increase and decrease was applied once, in record order. The running total ends at $2,095K after #1590.\n\nANSWER: $2095K",
